WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.200
MyCampusView Academy. Robotics 101, video 12: Uploading and testing.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.762
This is the big moment: your robot follows a real line.

3
00:00:10.812 --> 00:00:14.150
Let us make a good track first.

4
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.446
Use black electrical tape about two centimetres wide on white chart paper

5
00:00:21.496 --> 00:00:23.005
or a light floor.

6
00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:29.150
Start with gentle curves, and keep the track away from table edges.

7
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.605
Upload the line-follower sketch.

8
00:00:32.655 --> 00:00:36.799
Unplug the USB cable and switch the battery on.

9
00:00:36.849 --> 00:00:41.260
Place the robot with the line between the sensors.

10
00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:44.650
After two seconds it starts by itself.

11
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:51.008
On sharp corners, a gentle turn may not be enough.

12
00:00:51.058 --> 00:00:54.462
The robot runs off the corner.

13
00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:56.650
Watch what happens.

14
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:04.911
Now we set TURN_SPEED to minus 80, so the inner wheel spins backwards.

15
00:01:04.961 --> 00:01:11.150
The robot pivots around the corner and stays on the line.

16
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.906
When tuning, change one value at a time and write it down.

17
00:01:16.956 --> 00:01:20.639
If the robot overshoots, lower BASE_SPEED.

18
00:01:20.689 --> 00:01:26.150
If it misses sharp corners, lower TURN_SPEED, even below zero.

19
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:33.000
Next: Troubleshooting your robot.
